@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-cancellation-full-refund-at-recorded-but-not-used-to-prorate
+type: decision-log
+title: "Cancellation: full refund, at recorded but not used to prorate"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Context
+
+"Customers ask us to cancel their bookings" specifies `cancel(bookingId, at)` returning
+`{ bookingId, refund }`, that a cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment, and that a booking can
+only be cancelled once — but not how `refund` is computed, nor what role `at` plays in that computation.
+No cancellation-fee or proration policy exists anywhere in `README.md` or prior memory. dl-001 already
+anticipated the parameter: cancellation "will need 'now' at cancellation time, which will have to be
+threaded in explicitly (e.g. as a parameter) to keep honoring the determinism directive" — i.e. `at`
+exists so `cancel` never calls `Date.now()` itself, not because a specific refund formula was implied.
+
+## Decision
+
+- **Refund amount**: the booking's full `total`. No tiered or prorated refund (e.g. based on how close
+  `at` is to the booking's start) was introduced, since no such policy was requested anywhere; inventing
+  one would be a product decision this change is not asking for.
+- **Role of `at`**: recorded as the booking's new `cancelledAt` field (validated with the existing
+  `parseIsoDateTime`, the same boundary check `start`/`end` get), not used to vary the refund. This
+  satisfies "cancels the booking at the time `at`" literally (the instant is part of the booking's
+  state) while keeping the determinism directive's "no wall-clock" rule: the caller supplies "now"
+  instead of the service reading the clock.
+- **Freeing equipment**: `isFree` now also requires `cancelledAt === undefined` on top of the existing
+  overlap check, so a cancelled booking is immediately excluded from both `book`'s overlap check and
+  `availability`, for any period — not just from `at` onward. There is no partial/in-progress booking
+  state in this in-memory model, so "no longer holds its equipment" means a full, immediate release.
+- **One cancellation only**: `cancel` throws `Booking <id> is already cancelled` when `cancelledAt` is
+  already set, mirroring the `Unknown item`/`Item <id> cannot be rented by the hour` error style. An
+  unknown `bookingId` throws `Unknown booking: <id>` the same way.
+- **Representation**: `bookings[index]` is replaced with a new object (`{ ...booking, cancelledAt: at }`)
+  rather than mutated in place, keeping the existing immutable-update style used by `addEquipment`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `refund` is always equal to the original `total`; a future request for cancellation fees or
+  time-based proration would change only the `cancel` method, using `at` (already threaded through) to
+  compare against the booking's `start`/`end`.
+- `Booking` gained an optional `cancelledAt` field; nothing currently reads it except `isFree` and
+  `cancel`'s own already-cancelled check, so it carries no observable effect beyond those two paths and
+  the value echoed implicitly through `refund`.
+- Cancelling a booking well after its period has ended is still accepted and still refunds in full,
+  since no "already used" or expiry rule was requested; this would need to be revisited if the school
+  ever wants to disallow or discount cancellation after the rental period.
