@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+---
+id: task-005-let-customers-cancel-bookings
+type: task
+title: "Let customers cancel bookings"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Plans change, and customers ask us to cancel their bookings. Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental
+service: it cancels the booking at the time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`, the amount given
+back to the customer. A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment, and a booking can only be
+cancelled once.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added `cancel(bookingId, at)` to `RentalService` in `src/index.ts`, returning a new `Cancellation`
+  type (`{ bookingId, refund }`).
+- `Booking` gained an optional `cancelledAt` field, set on cancellation; `isFree` now also excludes
+  bookings with `cancelledAt` set, so a cancelled booking immediately stops blocking `book` and
+  `availability` for its item.
+- `cancel` validates `at` with the existing `parseIsoDateTime` boundary check, throws `Unknown booking:
+  <id>` for an unknown id, and throws `Booking <id> is already cancelled` if `cancelledAt` is already
+  set.
+- Refund is the booking's full `total`; no proration or cancellation fee was introduced, since none was
+  requested. See
+  `dl-004-cancellation-full-refund-at-recorded-but-not-used-to-prorate` (submitted, pending approval)
+  for the reasoning on the refund amount and the role of `at`.
+- Test-first: added 6 new tests (full refund on cancel, equipment freed for re-booking the same period,
+  equipment freed for `availability`, unknown booking, already-cancelled booking, invalid `at`),
+  confirmed they failed against the pre-change code (`service.cancel is not a function`), then
+  implemented until all 35 tests in `test/rental-service.test.ts` pass (`node --test`).
+- Updated `README.md`: documented the cancellation rule and `cancel`'s signature/errors, added a
+  `cancel` call to the usage example, and removed the "Cancellation is not implemented yet" line.
+
+## Notes
+
+No cancellation-fee or time-based proration policy was requested; `cancel` always refunds the full
+total regardless of how close `at` is to the booking's start or end. A future request for such a policy
+would only need to change `cancel`, which already has `at` and the booking's `start`/`end` on hand.
